#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f9a1aa-a390-574f-b1d7-d8bb1b97478b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 u^{2} - 12 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533012} {:answer/id #uuid "4134b830-3887-598c-b479-3d8b85171c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14 u^{2} + 4 uv - 6 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533031} {:answer/id #uuid "995a8e1a-95c0-5a99-b35d-f82c3964898a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 u^{2} - 4 uv + 4 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533057} {:answer/id #uuid "b48be496-3e3d-53b0-838c-eb6f4a85833a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533065} {:answer/id #uuid "c2fb8c43-78cf-570a-b762-20d95c71474e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 14 u^{2} + 12 uv - 2 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533069}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533065} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f31fcc4-3134-5b21-936a-7d9e43b33462" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9a222f71-5c1c-5947-8337-693d72d6ebf9" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨3 x - y,\\,- 2 x + y,\\,- z - 2⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2 x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $0\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,0\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- 4 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 u \\\\ 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 4 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3 x - y,\\,- 2 x + y,\\,- z - 2⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- 2 u + v,\\,- (2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}) - 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- 2 u + v,\\,- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- 2 u + v,\\,- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\cdot ⟨- 4 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3 u - v)\\cdot (- 4 u)+(- 2 u + v)\\cdot (4 v)+(- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 12 u^{2} + 4 uv- 8 uv + 4 v^{2}- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2 \\\\  & =- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3 x - y,\\,- 2 x + y,\\,- z - 2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "397a6974-dfac-52d9-b5df-0bc50361c68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} v + 2 uv^{2} + 3 uv + u - 2 v^{2} - 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533023} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6a532c-55a0-59d5-b070-81878ff0060b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v + 2 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 3 u - 2 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533033} {:answer/id #uuid "5b47b261-eaca-5315-bc67-d920b7c6ebbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 5 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533043} {:answer/id #uuid "661f9953-9c2c-5019-8928-9710c30593ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533045} {:answer/id #uuid "b4aae3d5-7110-5af4-87b3-e390ceb9db25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - 2 u + 2 v^{2} + 2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533066}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533045} :answer-field/id #uuid "460785b5-dfe6-5ff3-bd84-f6157544bae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "bbbc0ee0-272c-53fb-9af1-c9190cd9e631" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨2 z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=xy + x - y$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,uv + u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,v + 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & v + 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & v + 1 \\\\ 1 & u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & v + 1 \\\\ 0 & u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- v - 1,\\,1 - u,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2 z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=uv + u - v} \\\\  & =⟨2 (uv + u - v),\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨- v - 1,\\,1 - u,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(2 uv + 2 u - 2 v)\\cdot (- v - 1)+(uv)\\cdot (1 - u)+(u + v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 2 uv^{2} - 4 uv - 2 u + 2 v^{2} + 2 v- u^{2} v + uv+u + v \\\\  & =- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2 z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}(- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46954ab0-964a-57ab-8fa8-0e59d5360640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533304} {:answer/id #uuid "4cadc966-a1c1-5a9a-b852-d767b4eda976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 10 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533322} {:answer/id #uuid "61598bc1-09c8-541d-a2bc-495d7aa9e5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 30 \\\\ -3 & -15 \\\\ 9 & 45\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533363} {:answer/id #uuid "965ed177-569f-5e7f-8162-88c02d3a166d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}36 \\\\ -18 \\\\ 44\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533504} {:answer/id #uuid "a0550c2c-46e7-5b33-8b4a-ff7f9477e256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 30 \\\\ 3 & 15 \\\\ 9 & 45\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533528}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533363} :answer-field/id #uuid "843e0ee2-2793-547f-b5b3-9f47090c1d93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "26793c1a-40f5-5bd2-9877-7d31b77eb2ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-269383" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=3({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}3{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=3{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=3(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=3(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5\\end{bmatrix})=3(\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 15\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 30 \\\\ -3 & -15 \\\\ 9 & 45\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dad9073-478b-54b1-a7af-14e9b549d134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ 14 & 10 \\\\ -15 & -35\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533174} {:answer/id #uuid "0f783940-c57e-5b76-b2a2-204a0ec5ec07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 10 & -15 & -35\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533178} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1db3e7-b40d-5dd2-8056-ba5fbb14c5dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 30 \\\\ 18 & 45 \\\\ 42 & 105\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533520} {:answer/id #uuid "a46cedc9-7f50-57d8-8219-01fc7f258e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533537} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb01e9d-e482-500b-8961-81b00c565787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533637}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533637} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6ef3817-fd8a-50ea-a054-edd21587414d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "55449077-495e-5404-a705-ef8294705226" :question/math-academy-id "q-269371" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=3({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{3}3{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=3{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=3(y\\cdot {x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=3(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix})=3(\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 10 & -15 & -35\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 18 & 42 \\\\ 30 & -45 & -105\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7206ccb2-06f9-5d76-963e-53f626cd93e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533409}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533409} :answer-field/id #uuid "4961b210-cf39-5c5d-9780-93686b4c259c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c9c69b3-2459-5bbf-8e58-5df40a24a2f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533169}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533169} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ec0e1fd-84d9-5db8-b8ef-dcebc1ff50ce" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48db2235-143d-5295-b583-2370275dc856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533307}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533307} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5eddbec-fc63-5a81-8892-f999adcf5ee9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "77050388-523c-51b2-a4cd-6bc076f8c7c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-269479" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}(Ax-b)^{T}(Ax-b),$ where\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">\n${∇}_{A}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"3\" width=\"8px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"45px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"45px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td rowspan=\"3\" width=\"8px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-35$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWe can compute $\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}$ by applying the chain rule.\n\nLet $y=Ax-b\\in {R}^{3}.$ Then, $L(A)=\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}={\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}\n$$\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n{∇}_{y}L={∇}_{y}(\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{T}y)=y,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}={y}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWriting out $y=Ax-b$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\n{y}_{i}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}{a}_{ij}{x}_{j}-{b}_{i},\n$$\n\nwe have \n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}={x}_{j}$ if $i=k$, and\n\n- $\\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}}=0$ if $i\\ne k.$\n\nThis means that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}} & ={\\sum }_{k=1}^{3}\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{k}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{k}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂L}{∂{y}_{i}}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}\\cdot \\frac{∂{y}_{i}}{∂{a}_{ij}} \\\\  & ={y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $(i,j)$th entry of ${∇}_{A}L$ is the $i$th entry of $y$ multiplied by the $j$th entry of $x$, so\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=y\\cdot {x}^{T}.\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating ${∇}_{A}L$ at $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∇}_{A}L & =y\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(Ax-b)\\cdot {x}^{T} \\\\  & =(\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix})\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -70 \\\\ 0 & -35 \\\\ 0 & 63\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b61bf9-e784-5e7f-b97d-887c2be9e118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}36 & -84 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533147} {:answer/id #uuid "2b93066e-bfc5-5a06-b179-a89fa229c358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-18 & 42 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533247} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2431b9-469d-505f-9148-092565ac052a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}84 & -36 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 14 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533483} {:answer/id #uuid "96c28f9d-4d38-536d-af70-b7f7748daffc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -42 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533506} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e66d10-d942-55ef-95e9-74b83106f646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-36 & 84 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533738}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533738} :answer-field/id #uuid "88c7f20f-d80e-5b0b-9793-df75c33050d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "91187964-9e5b-5ba1-ba20-ee13e95e1abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-269386" :question/problem "Consider the function $L:{R}^{3\\times 2}\\to R$ defined by $L(A)=2({y}^{T}Ax)$ where \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${∇}_{A}L$ at \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of $L$ with respect to $A$ is a matrix of the same shape as $A$, with $(i,j)$th entry given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}},\n$$\n\nthe partial derivative of $L$ with respect to the $(i,j)$th entry of $A.$\n\nWriting out $L$ in component-wise notation as \n\n$$\nL={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}2{a}_{ij}{y}_{i}{x}_{j},\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂L}{∂{a}_{ij}}=2{y}_{i}{x}_{j}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${∇}_{A}L=2(y{x}^{T}).$\n\nEvaluating at the given values $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ we get\n\n$$\n{∇}_{A}L=2(\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 7\\end{bmatrix})=2(\\begin{bmatrix}-18 & 42 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}-36 & 84 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 14\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "277dde16-b64c-57ac-84b1-b5fcbd2bb63d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533237} {:answer/id #uuid "6ccb6452-a9e6-5252-8042-40dea1f911b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533396} {:answer/id #uuid "91580575-c469-5346-b827-2538c89c0475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533489} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e026ab-577b-5458-b42f-733bdaaa1c6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533736}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533489} :answer-field/id #uuid "15641ed6-e248-5cf5-b89d-0f633c218ee7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-fi